// Whai is DOM?

1. HTML code is also a document, So Document Object Model is the representation of HTML inside JS as nodes and objects.
2. In HTML the tags are represented as Nodes and objects in JS, so that we can access these elements and then manipulate it using the scripting language like JS.

Eg : -
HTML CODE - 

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>DOM Manipulation</title>
</head>
 <body>
    <h1 class = 'first'>DOM</h1>
    <p id="para">Lets learn more about DOM Manipulation</p>
    <div>
        <h3>Inner Heading</h3>
    </div>
 </body>
</html>

So DOM Tree of Above HTML COde is:-

    DOCUMENT
        |
    ___HTML____
   |           |
Head           Body                 -----> DOM Tree of corresponding HTM
  |             |                   -----> Here every Element will be represented as Node or Object, for  
Title       ____|____                       Manipulation using scripting langiage whenever reqd.        
           |    |    |
          H1    p    DIV
                      | 
                      H3

Now go on Console of above HTML Code:-
windows.document --> This will return the complete HTML

document.childNodes --> will return the childs of document i.e. <!DOCTYPE html>,<html>

document.children --> will return HTMLCollection i.e all Nodes in Document

document.body --> will retrun the body of document.

document.body.ChildNodes
--> This will return all the child nodes in body but here if we have spaces or text bw elements then after that element it will give text, And it also gives the id and class along with elements to which it is applied.
Above eg - [text,h1.first, text, p#para, text, div, text, commemnt, text, script, text]

document.body.children
-->HTMLCollection i.e. all elements inside body (will ignore text or spaces)
Above Eg - HTMLCollection(4) [h1.first, p#para , div, script, para:p#para]

document.body.firstChild
--> #text (gives from ChildNodes)

document.body.firstElementChild
--> <h1 class = "first"> DOM </h1>

